st=storypage('alone','THE ONE AND THE TYRANT','Ślokas 10.1–32',
 panels('Three panels: the Mothers merging into the Goddess; the fight in the sky; the sun shining on a peaceful world',[
  ('#fff3b0','“I AM ALONE”',DEVI(72,10,.6,False)+''.join(f'<g opacity=".5">{MOTHER(i,14+i*20,140,.25)}</g>' for i in range(7))),
  ('#2b2140','IN THE SKY',ASURA(50,110,.6,'#3a5a6a')+DEVI(100,10,.35,False)),
  ('#bfe3ff','PEACE',SUN(72,50,20)+'<path d="M0 150 q36 -10 72 0 t72 0 V190 H0z" fill="#4aa3df"/>')]),
 ['<b>The taunt.</b> Niśumbha is dead. Śumbha sneers: “You fight with the strength of others.”',
  '<b>The answer.</b> “I am alone in this world. Who else is there besides me?” Brahmāṇī and all the Mothers dissolve into her. “I stand alone. Stand firm.”',
  '<b>The duel.</b> Divine weapons against divine weapons; she breaks his with “huṃ”. Bow, spear, sword, shield, chariot, hammer: all cut. His fist meets her slap.',
  '<b>The sky.</b> He carries her into the sky; she fights “without support”. She whirls him round, hurls him down and pierces his chest with her trident.',
  '<b>Peace.</b> The sky clears, rivers flow in their courses, pure winds blow, the sun shines. Gods sing and dance.'],
 ("So all the goddesses were really one?","That's what she says, in her own words: ekaivāham, I alone. Brahmāṇī, Kālī, Vaiṣṇavī, all of them. The many forms are real, and they are one."),
 'Many forms, <b>one Goddess</b>.')
